ntinuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative. Therefore, we know there exists a function $f$ such that $∇f=F.$\n\nReconstructing $f$ from its gradient in the usual way, we get\n\n$$\nf=y{e}^{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the fundamental theorem for line integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =f(1,-1)-f(-1,1) \\\\  & =(-1){e}^{{1}^{2}}-(1){e}^{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-e-e \\\\  & =-2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363818 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363819 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363820 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363821 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363822 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1041 "selection" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363821 13194139535731 true] [17592186363817 1110 #uuid "26bfedf0-80d8-52d7-b46b-38f5bc532188" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363818 1034 "-e" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363818 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535731 true] [17592186363818 1111 #uuid "b6adea54-aa77-5b1a-a6f4-4a072c08d1ac" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363819 1034 "1-e" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535731 true] [17592186363819 1111 #uuid "dd64bdb8-9011-5f9e-bf89-276616b95938" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363820 1034 "2e-1" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363820 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535731 true] [17592186363820 1111 #uuid "02e4f1de-37de-51eb-8142-0bd8f0b378d2" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363821 1034 "-2e" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535731 true] [17592186363821 1111 #uuid "22af4294-2f71-50b2-8e9d-ea06db758751" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363822 1034 "e" 13194139535731 true] [17592