ependent of path.\n- $F$ is conservative." 13194139535731 true] [17592186363837 1113 #uuid "382b5216-f207-5094-bf02-ff591cd79a94" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363837 1145 "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨4t,\\,2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨4{t}^{2},\\,-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,\\,2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16{t}^{2}-8t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{t}^{2}-t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8{[\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =8[\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨{t}^{2},\\,-{t}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2t,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3})-0 \\\\  & =8-\\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative." 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363839 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363840 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363841 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363842 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186363843 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1041 "selection" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186363843 13194139535731 true] [17592186363838 1110 #uuid "11dfa3dd-5aad-5aed-bcca-cf232dee9173" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363839 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535731 true] [17592186363839 1111 #uuid "da5f6145-d8d9-5bca-be55-3a5d56ae41cf" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363840 1034 "I only" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535731 true] [17592186363840 1111 #uuid "4eb4e981-1d16-5904-98d4-8ecf16fa6105" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363841 1034 "II, III, and IV only" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535731 true] [17592186363841 1111 #uuid "b25bde75-2127-516a-ba9c-c4f2481e44a8" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363842 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535731 true] [17592186363842 1111 #uuid "9d531fa1-f63c-52ea-abe6-2d52ebebc6be" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363843 1034 "II only" 13194139535731 true] [17592186363843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535731 true] [17592186363843 1111 #uuid "06b598ac-2388-53f3-b916-ac5c5eb83af7" 13194139535731 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-125738" 17592186363809 "q-12573